1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Luke 22

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,480
So he consented and sought an opportunity to betray him to them in the absence of a crowd.

3
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:42,320
Then came the day of unleavened bread, on which the Passover lamb had to be sacrificed.

4
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:45,400
So Jesus sent Peter and John, saying,

5
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,320
Go and prepare the Passover for us, that we may eat it.

6
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:50,820
They said to him,

7
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:53,280
Where will you have us prepare it?

8
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:55,000
He said to them,

9
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:58,000
Behold, when you have entered the city,

10
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:00,000
a man carrying a jar of water will meet you.

11
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:04,580
Follow him into the house that he enters, and tell the master of the house,

12
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:06,340
The teacher says to you,

13
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:10,540
Where is the guest room, where I may eat the Passover with my disciples?

14
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:13,800
And he will show you a large upper room furnished.

15
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:15,240
Prepare it there.

16
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:18,520
And they went and found it just as he had told them,

17
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:20,320
and they prepared the Passover.

18
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:26,180
And when the hour came, he reclined at table, and the apostles with him.

19
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:27,460
And he said to them,

20
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:29,980
I have earnestly desired to eat the Passover,

21
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:32,320
and I will eat this Passover with you before I suffer.

22
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:37,680
For I tell you, I will not eat it until it is fulfilled in the kingdom of God.

23
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:41,440
And he took a cup, and when he had given thanks, he said,

24
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,560
Take this, and divide it among yourselves.

25
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:48,720
For I tell you that from now on I will not drink of the fruit of the vine

26
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:50,980
until the kingdom of God comes.

27
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:54,380
And he took bread, and when he had given thanks,

28
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,560
he broke it and gave it to them, saying,

29
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,860
This is my body, which is given for you.

30
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:02,480
Do this in remembrance of me.

31
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:06,300
And likewise the cup after they had eaten, saying,

32
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:10,900
This cup that is poured out for you is the new covenant in my blood.

33
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:16,600
But behold, the hand of him who betrays me is with me on the table.

34
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:19,900
For the Son of Man goes as it has been determined,

35
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:23,300
but woe to that man by whom he is betrayed.

36
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:26,020
And they began to question one another,

37
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:29,320
which of them it could be who was going to do this.

38
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:34,880
A dispute also arose among them as to which of them was to be regarded as the greatest.

39
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,680
And he said to them,

40
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:40,580
The kings of the Gentiles exercise lordship over them,

41
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:43,880
and those in authority over them are called benefactors.

42
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:45,980
But not so with you.

43
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:49,520
Rather, let the greatest among you become as the youngest,

44
00:02:49,980 --> 00:02:51,960
and the leader as one who serves.

45
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:57,400
For who is the greater, one who reclines at table or one who serves?

46
00:02:58,020 --> 00:02:59,960
Is it not the one who reclines at table?

47
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:06,720
a table? But I am among you, as the one who serves. You are those who have stayed with me

48
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:13,660
in my trials, and I assign to you, as my Father assigned to me, a kingdom, that you may eat and

49
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:18,920
drink at my table in my kingdom, and sit on thrones judging the twelve tribes of Israel.

50
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:28,200
Simon, Simon, behold, Satan demanded to have you, that he might sift you like wheat. But I have

51
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:34,160
prayed for you, that your faith may not fail, and when you have turned again, strengthen your

52
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:42,920
brothers. Peter said to him, Lord, I am ready to go with you both to prison and to death. Jesus

53
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:50,300
said, I tell you, Peter, the rooster will not crow this day until you deny three times that you know

54
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:57,920
me. And he said to them, When I sent you out with no money bag or knapsack or sandals, did you lack

55
00:03:57,920 --> 00:03:58,180
any?

56
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:06,860
They said, Nothing. He said to them, But now let the one who has a money bag take it,

57
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:12,240
and likewise a knapsack, and let the one who has no sword sell his cloak and buy one.

58
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:19,020
For I tell you, that this scripture must be fulfilled in me. And he was numbered with the

59
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:26,800
transgressors. For what is written about me has its fulfillment. And they said, Look, Lord,

60
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:28,180
here are two swords.

61
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:31,680
And he said to them, It is enough.

62
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:38,620
And he came out and went, as was his custom, to the Mount of Olives. And the disciples followed

63
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:45,440
him. And when he came to the place, he said to them, Pray that you may not enter into temptation.

64
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:51,140
And he withdrew from them about a stone's throw, and knelt down and prayed, saying,

65
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:57,720
Father, if you are willing, remove this cup from me. Nevertheless,

66
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:04,560
not my will, but yours be done. And there appeared to him an angel from heaven,

67
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:10,540
strengthening him. And being in an agony, he prayed more earnestly, and his sweat became

68
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:15,680
like great drops of blood falling down to the ground. And when he rose from prayer,

69
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:20,900
he came to the disciples and found them sleeping for sorrow. And he said to them,

70
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:27,400
Why are you sleeping? Rise and pray, that you may not enter into temptation.

71
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:32,400
While he was still speaking, there came a crowd, and the man called Judas,

72
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:38,500
one of the twelve, was leading them. He drew near to Jesus to kiss him. But Jesus said to him,

73
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:43,720
Judas, would you betray the Son of Man with a kiss?

74
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:47,680
And when those who were around him saw what would follow, they said,

75
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:53,720
Lord, shall we strike with the sword? And one of them struck the servant of the high priest and

76
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:56,740
cut off his right ear. But Jesus said,

77
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:58,180
No more of you.

78
00:05:58,180 --> 00:06:04,780
And he touched his ear and healed him. Then Jesus said to the chief priests and officers

79
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:10,040
of the temple and elders who had come out against him, Have you come out as against a robber,

80
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:15,940
with swords and clubs? When I was with you day after day in the temple, you did not lay hands

81
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:22,640
on me, but this is your hour and the power of darkness. Then they seized him and led him away,

82
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:27,180
bringing him into the high priest's house. And Peter was following at a distance.

83
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:28,160
And when they saw him, they said to him, What is this? And he said to them,

84
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:31,620
When they had kindled a fire in the middle of the courtyard and sat down together,

85
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:37,060
Peter sat down among them. Then a servant girl, seeing him as he sat in the light,

86
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:41,760
and looking closely at him, said, This man also was with him.

87
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:47,020
But he denied it, saying, Woman, I do not know him.

88
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:52,380
And a little later someone else saw him and said, You also are one of them.

89
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:56,280
But Peter said, Man, I am not.

90
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:58,140
And after an interval of a while, Peter said, I am not.

91
00:06:58,140 --> 00:07:00,700
And after an interval of about an hour, still another insisted, saying,

92
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:05,280
Certainly this man also was with him, for he too is a Galilean.

93
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:11,860
But Peter said, Man, I do not know what you are talking about.

94
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:16,400
And immediately, while he was still speaking, the rooster crowed.

95
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:21,720
And the Lord turned and looked at Peter. And Peter remembered the saying of the Lord,

96
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:25,900
how he had said to him, Before the rooster crows today,

97
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:27,900
you will deny me three times.

98
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:31,380
And he went out and wept bitterly.

99
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:37,300
Now the men who were holding Jesus in custody were mocking him as they beat him.

100
00:07:37,940 --> 00:07:40,540
They also blindfolded him and kept asking him,

101
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:44,700
Prophesy! Who is it that struck you?

102
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:48,540
And they said many other things against him, blaspheming him.

103
00:07:49,580 --> 00:07:53,280
When day came, the assembly of the elders of the people gathered together,

104
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:57,500
both chief priests and scribes, and they led him away to their council.

105
00:07:57,500 --> 00:08:01,740
And they said, If you are the Christ, tell us.

106
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:06,840
But he said to them, If I tell you, you will not believe.

107
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:09,480
And if I ask you, you will not answer.

108
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:15,980
But from now on the Son of Man shall be seated at the right hand of the power of God.

109
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:21,520
So they all said, Are you the Son of God then?

110
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:25,920
And he said to them, You say that I am.

111
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:27,480
Then they said,

112
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:31,140
What further testimony do we need?

113
00:08:31,460 --> 00:08:35,620
We have heard it ourselves from his own lips.

114
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:44,740
The End

